{
  "@context": {
    "schema": "https://schema.org/"
  },
  "@type": "Note",
  "@id": "note:notion-378",
  "title": "Changing the Engine",
  "status": "draft",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Changing the Engine"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "You change the engine by rewiring incentives. Here’s a blunt, workable package (actors + levers + verification)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. Enforceable conditionality on all guns + money"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Lever:** Apply U.S./EU arms-and-aid conditionality uniformly (Leahy vetting; AECA human-rights bars)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Mechanic:** “If X (civilian-harm threshold, settlement/rocket freeze) then aid continues; if not, it pauses automatically.” Publish unit-level vetting decisions. ([State](https://www.state.gov/bureau-of-democracy-human-rights-and-labor/releases/2025/01/leahy-law-fact-sheet?utm_source=chatgpt.com))"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. Put referees on the field, not just in statements"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Lever:** Stand-up a Hebron-style international presence again—but with a stronger mandate, body-cams, and public weekly incident reports."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Precedent:** TIPH (ended in 2019) shows the model; its removal showed the vacuum. ([Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temporary_International_Presence_in_Hebron?utm_source=chatgpt.com))"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. Hard verification zones and force limits"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Lever:** Extend “Sinai-style” demilitarized/verification zones to hot borders (with consent), with sensor grids and joint liaison rooms."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Precedent:** MFO in Sinai and IFOR/Dayton enforcement mechanics. ([Multinational Force and Observers](https://mfo.org/?utm_source=chatgpt.com))"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4. Hostage–prisoner exchange as a standing protocol"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Lever:** A permanent, third-party–verified swap framework (ICRC-style chain of custody, phased releases, inspection access) that isn’t renegotiated every crisis."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Mechanic:** Violations trigger automatic snap-backs in #1 and #3."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "5. Freeze-for-freeze with snap-back"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Lever:** Time-boxed freeze on settlement expansion and on projectile launches/force build-ups."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Mechanic:** Any breach = defined, pre-agreed penalties (aid pauses, customs preferences suspended) within 72 hours—no political discretion."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-18",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "6. Reconstruction escrow with clawbacks"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Lever:** Donor funds sit in escrow, released against milestones (utilities restoration, school reopenings) verified by the monitors in #2/#3."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-20",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Mechanic:** Diversion = automatic clawback + future tranche reduction."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-21",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "7. Security-sector reform with unit-level carrots"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-22",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Lever:** Training/equipment unlocked only after internal discipline outcomes are public (unit, offense, sanction)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-23",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Mechanic:** Mirrors Leahy compliance; measurable reduction in abuse incidents year-over-year. ([State](https://www.state.gov/bureau-of-democracy-human-rights-and-labor/releases/2025/01/leahy-law-fact-sheet?utm_source=chatgpt.com))"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-24",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "8. Power-sharing and consent architecture (the politics fix)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-25",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Lever:** Build a consociational, consent-based executive and policing board; minority vetoes on existential issues; sequencing elections after baseline security."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-26",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Precedent:** Good Friday institutions: power-sharing, police reform, consent principle, disarmament timelines. ([Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Good_Friday_Agreement?utm_source=chatgpt.com))"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-27",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "9. Truth + accountability track (narratives stop resetting wars)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-28",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Lever:** A standing truth-and-reconciliation process with limited amnesties tied to full disclosure and reparations, plus reopened emblematic cases."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-29",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Precedent:** South Africa’s TRC; renewed inquiries show longevity needs upkeep. ([Encyclopedia Britannica](https://www.britannica.com/topic/Truth-and-Reconciliation-Commission-South-Africa?utm_source=chatgpt.com))"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-30",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "10. Shared dashboards (sunlight as an incentive)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-31",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Lever:** Public, tamper-evident dashboards: civilian-harm counts, aid tranches, settlement starts, rocket launches, disciplinary actions, and verification alerts."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-32",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Mechanic:** Data feeds from #2/#3; thresholds wired to #1 snap-backs."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-33",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Why this works: it targets the **security dilemma** (fear loops) by pairing **credible monitoring** with **automatic, pre-agreed consequences**, not vibes or speeches. That’s how you change the game engine instead of “beating a boss.” ([Simon Fraser University](https://www.sfu.ca/~kawasaki/Jervis%20Cooperation.pdf?utm_source=chatgpt.com))"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}